   "reply": "`python tools/check.py` now passes with exit code 0. The one unit test passes, and no lines are over 100 characters.\n\nThe only thing it needed was a `NOTES_HOME` environment variable. `tools/check.py:25` reads `os.environ[\"NOTES_HOME\"]` and crashed with a `KeyError` when it wasn't set. I didn't change any code. I pointed `NOTES_HOME` at a new temporary directory for the run:\n\n```\nexport NOTES_HOME=\"$(mktemp -d)\"; python tools/check.py\n```\n\nThe script only prints that path, and the comment says the check harness uses it for scratch notes. Any writable directory will work. To run the checks yourself, set `NOTES_HOME` first, either in your shell profile or in CI.\n\nSeparately, line 27 of `check.py` is over 100 characters. The line-length check only scans `fieldnotes/**/*.py`, so it doesn't flag it.",
